From: Tiger Kaovilai <passawit.kaovilai@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] feat(cli): pin the server certificate by SHA-256 (--cert-sha256)

A client of a server with a self-signed certificate had one option on the
CLI: --insecure / Insecure = true, which turns certificate verification
off for the tunnel. tailbond pairs such servers by the SHA-256 of their
certificate, and Android already enforces that pin through
mqvpn_config_set_cert_verifier; the CLI (Linux, macOS) could not.

--cert-sha256 HEX / [Server] CertSHA256 (JSON "cert_sha256") now pins the
server: 64 hex digits, any case, ':'-separated or not. The shared
CLI->library bridge installs a verifier that accepts only a chain whose
leaf certificate (DER) hashes to the pin (constant-time compare; no chain
or hostname check, the pin is the identity), and turns insecure off, since
the library lets insecure override any verifier. The library consults the
verifier on every handshake (APP_VERIFY), so reconnects are checked too;
the paths of a multipath connection share its one handshake. On Windows
the store verifier is not installed over the pin.

A pin that is given must be valid, on the command line and in the file:
an empty or malformed --cert-sha256 (e.g. an unset $PIN), an empty
`CertSHA256 =`, or a JSON cert_sha256 that is not such a string is a
startup error, never "no pin", so it can't leave Insecure on or drop the
file's pin. The config parser records the key's presence
(cert_sha256_set) for that; the key is new, so no existing config has it.

- src/platform/cert_pin.{c,h}: parser and verifier (BoringSSL SHA256,
  CRYPTO_memcmp), compiled into the Linux, Darwin and Windows CLIs.
- tests/test_cert_pin.c: parser (case, colons, malformed), CLI/file
  resolution (empty, whitespace, odd length, non-hex on either side;
  through the real INI and JSON parsers for the file) and verifier (leaf
  only, one bit off, empty chain); test_config_bridge: a pin
  installs the verifier with the pin as context and forces insecure off.

Signed-off-by: Tiger Kaovilai <passawit.kaovilai@gmail.com>
